 "rules": [
  "1 (\u00a767): section onset = the first characteristic attack - first attack-cluster after the container opens whose level jump crosses a threshold scaled to the section's own peak. Validated at 43.93.",
  "2 (\u00a770): a wind/suction percept lives in an unbroken decay - opens at the last attack's release, runs while spectral flux stays low, closes at the next brightness jump. Validated at 66.497/68.31; first hunt 171.91-173.96.",
  "3 (candidate, \u00a774): quiet timbral entries defeat rule 1 - J's 6.875 has no level attack (nearest is 7.94); some sections enter by timbre, needing a spectral-change detector. Undesigned.",
  "1a (refinement, \u00a775): what 'onset' means depends on context - at the top of the piece J wants the FIRST AUDIBLE SOUND (0.43, quieter than rule 1's threshold caught at 0.68), while at a mid-piece change over faint transitional material he wants the first CHARACTERISTIC attack (43.93). Two targets, one word.",
  "4 (\u00a780, the masking law): at a section entry over a decaying predecessor, scheduled events are masked until the tail falls below them; a section's ear-onset is its first PUNCH-THROUGH. Unifies 43.93, 6.875, 22.88. Detectable as a floor-crossing - the AI pass can propose every remaining section's ear-onset. Fix pattern: substrate starts at the ear onset; masked entry grains stay sand, whose bursts sit below perception (\u00a777)."
 ]
}